{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And to Moses He said: ascend to YHWH.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): this is before the giving of the Torah, and from this it says, ״ונגש משה לבדו אל ה׳״ — 'and Moses alone shall draw near to YHWH' — and the clarification of אל עב הענן, 'to the thick darkness of the cloud,' and this is the language that is said (Exodus 20): ״ומשה נגש אל הערפל״ — 'and Moses drew near to the fog' — for that passage too, of 'and the people saw the voices,' was before the giving of the Torah." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: 'and to Moses He said' — the designated Name; 'ascend to YHWH' — this is Metatron, whose name is like the name of his Master; and so the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded. And he is called by this name because in this name are included two expressions indicating his nature, namely 'master' and 'emissary': 'master' in the language of the Sages, who call the mistress who holds authority מטרונא; 'emissary' in Greek, who call an emissary מנטטור. And it further includes a third sense, of guarding, for the translation of משמרת is מטרת; and because he is the guardian of the world he is called the Guardian of Israel." "<b>And behold,</b> from the instruction of his name we have grasped that he is master over everything beneath him, for all the host above and below — are they not in his domain and under his hand; and he is the emissary to the one above him and beyond him, who gave him authority over all, and his name is master of His house and ruler over all His possessions." "<b>And you should</b> know that according to the connotation of the word אדון, the letter tet in the name should be doubled; and the reason for the doubling of the tet is that two tets equal ח״י (18), and what remains in the name is מרון, which is אדון. Or the doubling of the tet may be because it is the tenth pillar drawing power from the nine; and behold, it is written in certain places by the masters of the Kabbalah with an added yod — sometimes called by six letters, corresponding to the six extremities, and sometimes by seven. And it is well known that he is called נער, and therefore Scripture mentioned the firstborn of Israel by the name נערים, as it says (Exodus 24): ״וישלח את נערי בני ישראל״." "<b>And you should</b> know that this ascent was not now required on behalf of Aaron and his sons and the seventy elders; and what it says, ״ונגש משה לבדו אל ה׳״ — 'and Moses alone shall draw near to YHWH' — the intention is upon Metatron as well. And the verse ought to have said ונגשת לבדך — 'and you alone shall draw near' — for the designated YHWH is the one speaking, and this utterance is to Moses alone, for He said to him: 'ascend to YHWH, you and Aaron, Nadav and Avihu, and seventy of the elders of Israel, and you shall prostrate yourselves from afar.' And the reason it speaks in the third person — 'and Moses alone shall draw near to YHWH' — is perhaps that the one saying 'and Moses alone shall draw near to YHWH' is Metatron himself, who said this concerning himself; and it is the language of a charge, commanding Aaron, Nadav and Avihu, and seventy of the elders of Israel; and it immediately adjoins to it: ״ויראו את אלהי ישראל״ — 'and they saw the Elohim of Israel.' And Moses alone drew nearer still, for thus it was said to him: ״עלה אלי ההרה והיה שם״ — 'ascend to Me to the mountain and be there' — and this ascent was for additional attainment, until he came within the cloud, as it says: ״ויבא משה בתוך הענן״ — 'and Moses came within the cloud.'" "<b>And you already</b> know that this angel is the one that led Elisha astray in his matter and caused him to stumble into doubting the two authorities, and he went out to a bad culture, and so everyone who is not careful in his matter — behold, he sins against his own soul and brings upon himself a pitfall and great guilt for which no atonement is possible. And it seems to me that for this reason the section of 'ואל משה אמר' was joined to the word 'מוקש,' for its matter, for one who is not careful concerning it, is a place of error in which the first father was ensnared and caught, also the sons in the wilderness, also Nadav and Avihu; and the perfect righteous man, R. Akiva, who was careful in its matter, entered in peace and came out in peace — and this is what was expounded of it (Deuteronomy 33): ״ואתה מרבבות קדש״ — it is a sign in his 'ten thousand' (רבבה); YHWH of hosts is His name; He is a master (אדון) in His host (צבא). And understand this."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {3 "The gematria of two tets (טט = 9+9 = 18 = ח״י) and the remainder מרון = אדון are rendered exactly as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:42.739156726Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}